3. 📏 Feature Importance (and its traps)
Built-in importance (tree models)
• gain: average loss reduction from splits on the feature (most useful)
• weight / split: how often it is used (misleading)
• cover: samples affected by its splits
Trap: built-in importance is computed on training data and is biased toward high-cardinality and continuous features.
Permutation importance
Shuffle one feature on held-out data and measure how much the score drops. Model-agnostic and computed on data the model has not seen.
from sklearn.inspection import permutation_importance

r = permutation_importance(pipe, X_val, y_val, n_repeats=10,
                           scoring="average_precision", random_state=42)

for i in r.importances_mean.argsort()[::-1][:10]:
    print(X_val.columns[i], r.importances_mean[i], r.importances_std[i])
WARNING: With correlated features, shuffling one leaves its twin to fill in, so both look unimportant. Group correlated features, or drop one, before reading results.
