10. 🧪 Practical Project
Dataset: your Day 10 tuned and calibrated XGBoost model (fraud, churn or loan default).
Steps
1. Compute built-in gain, permutation importance (validation, PR-AUC) and mean |SHAP|. Compare the three rankings
2. Draw PDP + ICE for the top 3 features. Which show interactions?
3. Verify a monotonic constraint with a PDP (Day 10)
4. Build a SHAP beeswarm and 3 waterfalls: one true positive, one false positive, one false negative
5. Explain the same 3 cases with LIME. Do they agree with SHAP?
6. Fit a depth-3 surrogate tree and report its fidelity
7. Check for leakage and for proxy features. Retrain after removing any suspect column and compare PR-AUC
