11. 📝 Cheat Sheet
• Global = what the model uses overall. Local = why this one prediction
• Built-in importance is biased. Prefer permutation (on validation) or SHAP
• PDP = average effect, ICE = per-sample, ALE = best when features correlate
• SHAP: prediction = base + sum(SHAP). Trees use TreeExplainer, classifier output is log-odds
• Explain transformed features and sum dummy columns back to the original feature
• LIME is fast and model-agnostic but unstable. Always repeat
• Surrogate trees need a fidelity check
• Counterfactuals give recourse: "what would change the decision?"
• A surprising top feature usually means leakage. Check before celebrating
• Explanations describe the model, not reality: correlation, not causation
